 "_comment_fxl": "FX-L (2026-11-08, REVIEW_LOGIC B2 / M8): a business is classified on its OWN text, never on the search it was found on, so the business and list cases now carry the public titles their results showed on the stored readings (seo_rank_history snapshots, page titles only). The negative cases below are businesses on a service results page that are not competitors (an off-category business ranking on a city word): they must never come out direct.",
 "_comment_fxl7": "FX-L section 7 (2026-11-10): the hosts the first production Trial classified, labelled from the evidence the run held (the titles of their results; most addresses were Google redirects, so no path). Rule behind the labels: a job board / recruiter / staffing firm, a news or update site, a directory, a training provider or school is never a competitor; `direct` needs provider evidence (a service page of its own, or a homepage naming the client's services), otherwise a business on topic is `adjacent` (a close competitor to confirm). Every third new case is hold-out."
